      "start_seconds": 1.11,
      "end_seconds": 2.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "Good afternoon, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.4,
      "end_seconds": 10.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "No problem at all, come in. What's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.43,
      "end_seconds": 18.48,
      "duration_seconds": 6.05,
      "text": "So the thing is, I've got being found cold and drowsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.65,
      "end_seconds": 22.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.14,
      "end_seconds": 32.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.84,
      "end_seconds": 61.25,
      "duration_seconds": 7.41,
      "text": "Okay: temperature is 36.6 degrees, pulse is 84 beats a minute, BP is 112 over 75."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.03,
      "end_seconds": 64.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.74,
      "end_seconds": 69.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "I'll come back to the numbers."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.55,
      "end_seconds": 80.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "Did it it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.79,
      "end_seconds": 94.11,
      "duration_seconds": 12.32,
      "text": "Probably six months. Yeah. I didn't wanna make a fuss, you know. Oh, and slurred speech. Had that since last Tuesday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.36,
      "end_seconds": 102.05,
      "duration_seconds": 6.69,
      "text": "have you had being found cold and drowsy before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.89,
      "end_seconds": 108.9,
      "duration_seconds": 5.01,
      "text": "A bit, last year. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.32,
      "end_seconds": 126.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "and what about alcohol, fall or head injury?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.63,
      "end_seconds": 131.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "No, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.37,
      "end_seconds": 134.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Is your digestion otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.23,
      "end_seconds": 137.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.92,
      "end_seconds": 143.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.69,
      "end_seconds": 155.4,
      "duration_seconds": 10.71,
      "text": "An underactive thyroid, for about a year a neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.1,
      "end_seconds": 157.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.07,
      "text": "Hm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.85,
      "end_seconds": 162.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "I've had low haemoglobin for about a year now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.79,
      "end_seconds": 179.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.18,
      "end_seconds": 185.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.56,
      "text": "Plasters. I come out in... well, a red itchy rash"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.53,
      "end_seconds": 192.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.5,
      "end_seconds": 217.73,
      "duration_seconds": 21.23,
      "text": "Thyroxine. I take it 75 micrograms, every morning for my thyroid. Oh, I'm supposed to take it regularly, but I don't always manage. Iron tablets. I take it once a day for my blood count."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.81,
      "end_seconds": 222.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Have you had any surgical procedures?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 224.09,
      "end_seconds": 229.72,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "Oh, I had my tonsils removed as a teenager."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.31,
      "end_seconds": 233.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.9,
      "end_seconds": 252.25,
      "duration_seconds": 13.35,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. I swim twice a week. I work in accounts at a hospital."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.27,
      "end_seconds": 257.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "let me look at the area, I'll be gentle"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 259.69,
      "end_seconds": 261.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "yes, that's fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.86,
      "end_seconds": 264.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "I'm just checking this side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.54,
      "end_seconds": 280.56,
      "duration_seconds": 8.02,
      "text": "Your temperature is twenty-nine degrees, your skin is ice cold and your pulse is very slow."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.92,
      "end_seconds": 303.95,
      "duration_seconds": 21.03,
      "text": "You can relax now. Putting it all together, it points towards severe hypothermia. I want blood tests done, that's for hypothermia. I want a blood sugar done, that's for hypothermia. Handle gently and warm slowly with warm blankets and warm fluids through the drip."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.16,
      "end_seconds": 309.98,
      "duration_seconds": 5.82,
      "text": "Sure. Come back straight away. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 310.69,
      "end_seconds": 314.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.12,
      "end_seconds": 317.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Look after yourself."
    }
  ]
